{"seconds": 41.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect. Ng6+ is clearly the best move, forcing the king out and then Nxf8+ wins the rook with a strong attack. The main line is: Ng6+ Kg7 (or Kg8) Nxf8+ Kh8 (or Kf7) Qg7# (or continuing with a winning position).\n\n**Best move:** Ng6+\n\n**Main line:** Ng6+ Kg7 Nxf8+ Kh8 Qg7+ Nxg7 Rxg7\n\n**Motif:** fork\n\n**Explanation:** After Black's Nf5, White's knight on e5 can leap to g6 with check, forking the king and rook on f8. Black's king must move (Kg7 or Kg8), allowing Nxf8+ which wins the rook with continuing threats. If Kg7 Nxf8+ Kh8, then Qg7# is checkmate\u2014the queen is protected by the rook on g3. This teaches you to look for knight moves that create forcing checks and simultaneously attack loose pieces, especially rooks near the king.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Ng6+\", \"line\": [\"Ng6+\", \"Kg7\", \"Nxf8+\", \"Kh8\", \"Qg7+\", \"Nxg7\", \"Rxg7\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21", "move": "Nf7+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21", "move": "Ng6+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21", "move": "Qxf5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2NQ2/3PpP2/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 b - - 0 21", "move": "exf5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2NQ2/3PpP2/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 b